    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0043a21e7784db2aeb5e2efbc6b356686e4b6d04e750fdc74a8e0c49f6d08886",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The upper and lower arguments realize the same free-energy mechanism from opposite directions. Upper bounds control the volume of points above height gamma and optimize entropy plus beta-weighted amplitude, with the optimizer reaching the maximal-height boundary in the frozen phase. Lower bounds impose simultaneous prime-block exceedances, prove that the resulting high-point volume has the matching entropy by a genealogically organized second moment, and optimize the same tradeoff. For theta<0, removing the shared prime trunk changes the effective variance but leaves this variational architecture intact.",
